{
  "analysis": "The binary runs successfully with `node vm.js`! Doom initializes, finds doom.wad, and starts loading. However, it terminates early at PC=0x1b4d8 after 4.6M instructions, right after \"R_InitSprites: Sprite TROO : A : 1 has two lumps mapped to it\". I need to check what instruction is at that PC and whether /tmp/frame.bmp was created.",
  "plan": "Check if /tmp/frame.bmp exists, disassemble the code around PC=0x1b4d8 to understand why it terminated, and use addr2line to identify the source function.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null || echo \"No frame file\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-objdump -d /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -B2 -A2 '1b4d8:'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-addr2line -e /app/doomgeneric_mips -f 0x1b4d8\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
